IMPORT prelude

-- Payment Services Act 2019 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence: the prohibition (s 5), the licence classes and the major payment
-- institution thresholds (s 6), exempt providers (s 13), and the services that are not payment services (First Schedule Part 2).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSA2019.txt (amendments to
-- Act 1 of 2021, in force 4 April 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 16 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the licensing perimeter. Not
-- encoded: the licensing process, conduct and safeguarding duties (ss 18 to 24), interoperability, control of licensees, audit,
-- Part 3 onwards, and the prescribed amounts (in regulations, not retrieved) including the e-money account caps of s 24.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Payment Services Act 2019 -- licensing`

§§ `5 -- the prohibition`

-- s 5(1): no one may "carry on a business of providing any type of payment service in Singapore" without a licence or an
-- exemption. (2): a person who provides a payment service while carrying on ANY business "is presumed to carry on a secondary
-- business of providing that ... payment service, regardless whether [it] is related or incidental to the primary business", and
-- (b) the presumption "is NOT REBUTTED by proof that [it] is related or incidental".
-- (3): an individual -- a fine up to $125,000 or 3 years; anyone else -- up to $250,000.
--
-- A shop that offers to send customers' money home as a sideline is carrying on a payment-service business, and saying it is
-- only incidental to the shop is no answer.
GIVEN `provides the service as a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `provides it alongside another business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person carries on a payment service business` IF
    `provides the service as a business` OR `provides it alongside another business`

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed business` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 125000 ELSE 250000

§§ `First Schedule Part 2, 13 -- outside the Act`

-- First Schedule Part 2 para 2: not payment services include (a) a COMMERCIAL AGENT paying on behalf of a buyer or seller; (b)
-- cheques, cashier's orders, postal orders; (e) payments between related corporations not through an outside provider; (f) cash
-- transport; (g) FREE, not-for-profit or charitable collection and delivery of cash; (h) a technical service provider that "does
-- not at any time enter into possession of any money"; (i) payments solely incidental to a business regulated under the FAA,
-- Insurance Act, SFA or Trust Companies Act; (j) LIMITED PURPOSE e-money (store cards, loyalty points); (l) limited purpose digital
-- tokens.
-- s 13(1): exempt from licensing -- banks, merchant banks, finance companies, and licensed card issuers.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `remitting money abroad for customers for a fee`
    `running a money-changing counter`
    `operating a crypto exchange`
    `issuing a mall gift card usable only at the mall`
    `a payment gateway that never holds the money`
    `a sales agent collecting payment for the seller`
    `intra-group payments within a corporate group`
    `a charity carrying cash donations free of charge`
    `a bank offering remittances`
    `a secure cash-in-transit company`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs a licence` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `remitting money abroad for customers for a fee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `running a money-changing counter` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `operating a crypto exchange` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6 -- which licence`

-- s 6(3): a money-changing service alone needs a money-changing licence (or a payment institution licence).
-- (4): ONE of account issuance, domestic transfer, cross-border transfer, merchant acquisition, e-money issuance or digital payment
-- token service, or TWO OR MORE services including money-changing, needs a STANDARD or MAJOR payment institution licence.
-- (5): a MAJOR payment institution licence is required where (a) the monthly average (over a calendar year) of transactions
-- "exceeds $3 million ... for any one" of the non-e-money services, or "$6 million ... for 2 or more"; or (b), (c) the daily
-- average e-money float exceeds $5 million.
DECLARE Business HAS
    `money-changing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other payment services` IS A NUMBER
    `highest monthly average for one service` IS A NUMBER
    `monthly average across all services` IS A NUMBER
    `daily average e-money float` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the business` IS A Business
GIVETH A STRING
`the licence needed` MEANS
    IF     `the business`'s `highest monthly average for one service` GREATER THAN 3000000
       OR  (`the business`'s `other payment services` AT LEAST 2 AND `the business`'s `monthly average across all services` GREATER THAN 6000000)
       OR  `the business`'s `daily average e-money float` GREATER THAN 5000000
    THEN "major payment institution licence"
    ELSE IF `the business`'s `other payment services` AT LEAST 1
         THEN "standard payment institution licence"
         ELSE IF `the business`'s `money-changing` THEN "money-changing licence" ELSE "none"
